ight would shift toward purely algorithmic verification. However, until such provability exists, replacing human judgment with black-box autonomy is a reckless gamble with public safety. Policy must mandate heterogeneous failovers, ensuring that technical progress remains strictly conditional on our ability to halt systems that deviate from human-defined safety parameters. 🛡️",
